+Hallucinated/inaccurate parts:
+The document describes /send-message, /status, /config, and /analytics as Discord slash commands. The actual commands (from commandDocs.ts and index.ts) are completely different — /register, /whois, /slots, /war_range_targets, etc. None of those four exist.
+The "Discord Heartbeat" background job (discordHeartbeat running every 30 seconds) doesn't exist in the code at all.
+The analytics endpoints described (/analytics) are real, but the document misattributes them — they live under /analytics/v2/l/:shortId and /analytics/v2/p/:messageId, not /l/:shortId and /p/:messageId as top-level routes (though the v1 analytics router also exists separately).
+The document says the QueuedNation model is "shared between both systems" (queuing and Discord bot). In reality the Discord bot (discord-bot/) is a completely separate Node process with its own codebase and has no shared models with the server.
+The data flow description in section 10 mixes up the two separate systems as if they're one integrated application, when they're actually two independent services that communicate only via HTTP.

