+
+---
+
+## bar3-client Architecture
+
+The client is a Vue 3 single-page application built with Vuetify 3 (dark theme, orange primary), TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. It is deployed as a static site (Render) with all routes rewritten to `index.html`.
+
+### Authentication & Session Model
+
+Two independent auth layers coexist:
+
+- **Discord OAuth2** (`discordAuth`): The primary gate. The server handles the OAuth exchange and sets a session cookie. The client checks `/auth/session` once per page load and caches the result in `sessionStorage`. Role flags (`bar3Client`, `bar3Server`, `memberGuild`) drive route guards and sidebar visibility.
+- **PnW API Key** (`v2Api`): A secondary credential stored in `localStorage` and sent as `x-api-key`. Required for message sending, automation, and template management. Login hits `/api/v2/auth/login`; the resulting session is server-side.
+
+The router guards redirect unauthenticated users to `/auth/login` and enforce per-route role requirements (`requiresClientAccess`, `requiresMemberAccess`, `requiresBotAuth`).
+
+### State Management (Vuex)
+
+A single flat store holds: application on/off toggle, sent messages, API usage details, server/client versions, update availability, Discord auth state, and role flags. An `analytics` submodule holds legacy campaign data. There are no async Vuex actions; all async work is done in components or composables before committing mutations.
+
+### API Communication
+
+Three fetch wrappers handle different concerns:
+
+- `apiFetch` — attaches the PnW API key header and `credentials: include`; used by legacy v1 endpoints.
+- `v2Fetch` (internal to `v2Api`) — same pattern, used for all `/api/v2/*` endpoints.
+- `botFetch` (internal to `botApi`) — uses `AUTH_BASE_URL` which can differ from `API_BASE_URL` to support Safari's same-site cookie restriction via a reverse proxy.
+
+URL roots are resolved from env vars (`VUE_APP_API_URL`, `VUE_APP_AUTH_URL`, `VUE_APP_SERVER_URL`) with `window.location.origin` as the fallback.
+
+### Views & Routing
+
+| Route | Access | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `/dashboard` | Client | Sent messages, API usage charts, refresh button |
+| `/automation` | Client | Bulk send tools (active+unallied, Discord filter, by nation ID) |
+| `/config` | Client | API key, update interval, analytics toggle |
+| `/message-creator` | Client | WYSIWYG (Quill) and advanced (HTML/CSS + juice inlining) editors |
+| `/analytics` | Client | v2 analytics graph + legacy campaign view |
+| `/account` | Client | PnW API key login/logout |
+| `/nation` | Member | Registered nation details and defensive war table |
+| `/alliance` | Member | Alliance stats and counter-war request UI |
+| `/bot` | Admin | Bot server list, command usage, send-message panel |
+| `/constitution` | Member | Rendered constitution with ToC, search, dark mode |
+| `/about`, `/help` | Public | Static informational pages |
+| `/auth/discord/callback` | Public | Finalises OAuth and redirects |
+
+### Message Editor Pipeline
+
+The message creator supports two modes selected by a tab:
+
+- **Basic**: Quill editor → raw HTML fragment.
+- **Advanced**: Hand-written HTML + CSS → inlined via `juice` → preview via `PreviewMessage`.
+
+Both paths pass output through `sanitizeHtml`, which uses a `<template>` element to parse and walk the DOM, blocking dangerous tags (`script`, `iframe`, `form`, etc.), stripping `on*` event attributes, sanitising `style` values, and rejecting unsafe URL schemes. The inlined HTML is saved to both the legacy config endpoint and, if a v2 session exists, to MongoDB via `/api/v2/templates`.
+
+### Analytics
+
+The `Analytics` view merges two data sources: v2 analytics fetched from `/analytics/v2/me` (transformed into a synthetic `AnalyticalCampaign` object for reuse by `AnalyticsGraphCard`) and the legacy campaign system (`/analytics/campaigns`). Charts are rendered by `vue-chartjs` wrapping Chart.js, with custom daily-bucketing logic applied client-side.
+
+### Constitution Renderer
+
+The constitution page is a self-contained rendering pipeline:
+
+1. `constitutionSource.ts` fetches from a configured Google Doc via the backend, falling back to the bundled `constitution.md`.
+2. `constitutionRenderer.ts` parses the markdown line-by-line, extracting `:::law`, `:::lore`, and `:::amendment` container blocks into a typed `ConstitutionBlock[]` array.
+3. A table of contents is built by scanning headings outside containers; slugs are deduplicated with a counter map.
+4. The view renders blocks using three specialised components (`LawBlock`, `LoreBox`, `AmendmentNote`) and plain `v-html` for prose. An `IntersectionObserver` drives scroll-spy ToC highlighting. Full-text search operates over a pre-built index of section text extracted at render time.
+----- APPEND BLOCK END -----

